constants editorDirectives
; @public
; Editor directives cheat sheet.
; Literal examples below use "@ name" so they stay visible as text.
; @tab 82
;
; Global editor directives
; @ config color.<path> <value>	Override a named editor color.
; @ config font <font>	Change the editor font.
; @ config export.fileName <fileName>	Set the export file name for the project.
; @ config bin.<id>.url <url>	Define a binary asset URL.
; @ config bin.<id>.memory <memoryId>	Load a binary asset into memory.
; @ config keyboard.keyCodeMemory <memoryId>	Store keyboard key codes in a module memory.
; @ config keyboard.keyPressedMemory <memoryId>	Store pressed-key state in a module memory.
; @ config runtime <runtimeId>	Select the runtime backend for the project.
;
; Code block directives
; @ alwaysOnTop	Keep the block rendered above normal blocks.
; @ button <memoryTarget> [offValue] [onValue]	Add a momentary button widget.
; @ bars <pointerSource> <elementCount> [minValue maxValue]	Draw vertical bars over a typed pointer range.
; @ disabled	Mark the block as disabled.
; @ favorite	Mark the block as a favorite.
; @ group <name> [nonstick]	Group blocks together for dragging behavior.
; @ hide	Collapse the rest of the block behind "...".
; @ home	Mark the block as the home/starting focus target.
; @ meter <typedValueSource> [minValue maxValue]	Render a horizontal level meter.
; @ nth	Show the module's compile order number.
; @ opacity <0..1>	Set the block opacity.
; @ piano <pressedKeysListTarget> <pressedKeyCountTarget> [startingMidiNote]	Render a piano keyboard widget.
; @ plot <pointerSource> <elementCount> [minValue maxValue]	Plot a typed pointer range.
; @ public	Mark the block exported by a module file.
; @ wave <pointerSource> <elementCount> [absolutePointerSource]	Draw a waveform over a typed absolute pointer range.
; @ wave2 <pointerSource> <elementCount> [absolutePointerSource]	Draw a waveform at double height.
; @ wave4 <pointerSource> <elementCount> [absolutePointerSource]	Draw a waveform at quadruple height.
; @ slider <memoryTarget> [min] [max] [step]	Add a slider widget.
; @ switch <memoryTarget> [offValue] [onValue]	Add a toggle switch widget.
; @ tab <position1> <position2> ...	Define visual tab stops for literal tab characters.
; @ viewport <top-left|top-right|bottom-left|bottom-right>	Anchor the block to a viewport corner.
; @ watch <memoryExpression>	Show a runtime watch value.
; alias: @ w <memoryExpression>	Short alias for @ watch.
;
; Notes
; memoryTarget is name or module:name; pointerSource is a pointer memory or &buffer.
; elementCount is a positive integer, an integer memory target, or count(memoryTarget).
; @ watch can also be written as a trailing comment on a code line.
; @ config memory values may be local in module blocks or module-qualified from any block.

constantsEnd
